sequenceDiagram
    participant VSCode as VS Code<br/>(MCP Client)
    participant MCPServer as Your MCP Server
    participant Proxy as OAuth Proxy
    participant User as User
    participant APS as APS

    Note over MCPServer,Proxy: Same origin: <PUBLIC_URL>

    VSCode->>MCPServer: Connect to /mcp
    MCPServer-->>VSCode: 401 Unauthorized

    VSCode->>MCPServer: GET /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp
    MCPServer-->>VSCode: authorization_servers: [<PUBLIC_URL>]
    Note over VSCode,MCPServer: Authorization server (proxy) is on the same domain

    VSCode->>Proxy: GET /.well-known/oauth-authorization-server
    Proxy-->>VSCode: auth server metadata

    VSCode->>Proxy: GET /authorize?redirect_uri=vscode.dev/redirect&...
    Proxy->>APS: Redirect to APS authorize (redirect_uri=<PUBLIC_URL>/auth/callback)
    APS->>User: Show sign-in / consent screen
    User->>APS: Signs in and consents
    APS->>Proxy: GET /auth/callback?code=<APS code>
    Proxy->>APS: POST /token with APS code
    APS-->>Proxy: APS access + refresh token
    Note over Proxy: Caches  APS credentials in memory
    Note over Proxy: Creates  its own temporary MCP code

    Proxy->>VSCode: Redirect to vscode.dev/redirect?code=<MCP code>
    VSCode->>Proxy: POST /token with MCP code
    Proxy-->>VSCode: MCP access token (opaque, 1h TTL)

    VSCode->>MCPServer: Connect to /mcp with MCP token
    Note over MCPServer,Proxy: MCP token → APS token

    MCPServer->>APS: Call Data Management API with APS token
    APS-->>MCPServer: data
    MCPServer-->>VSCode: tool result